  "claim_boundary": "V4 adds a persistent local operator around the certified V3 harness. It preloads one immutable Atom wiki and graph RAG snapshot plus one supervised resident Qwen lane before accepting traffic, then publishes every answer through the existing atomic V3 artifact transaction. The browser surface is loopback-only, authenticated in memory, and places the real committed artifact beside conversation controls. Atom still owns facts, retrieval, grounding, abstention, and memory. This does not claim that an LLM creates facts, that all questions are answerable, that every GGUF is compatible, that cloud routing is enabled, or that retired language-model distillation is active."
